255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(Area Condition)/Pg 15 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

256 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(This area was predominantly clean with few littered areas. The streets were very well painted with adequate lighting and pedestrian areas. However many houses had arrays of set-ups in their yards as well as various house builds indicating the lack of an HOA. This could provide a hurdle to community outreach. There were numerous public street signs and road signs.  )/Pg 15 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

257 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(Street Presence)/Pg 15 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

258 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(There were numerous individuals walking, using bicycles, and public transport. A wheelchair resident was even seen using the public crosswalks and crossing busy intersections. It was noted that there were very limited smart crosswalks. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

259 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(Stores & Food Access)/Pg 15 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

260 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(There were very limited number of grocery stores and fresh produce stores available. Instead there were small businesses with small grocery stores and limited selection of food. There were numerous water filling stations around the community. There are more convenience stores as opposed to major grocery stores. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

